// RUN: python3 %S/Inputs/check_vunzip_vzip_validation.py

// The public Python surface must reject unsupported vunzip/vzip shapes before
// they reach the C++ verifier: source width outside 16/32, a half-width target
// that is not exactly half, a non-vreg or shape-mismatched vzip high operand,
// a half width outside 8/16, and a wide target that is not exactly 2x.
// The helper also checks the accepted default and explicit-to_dtype shapes.
